v></div><div class="mod-bar" data-mid="m3" data-openmod="m3"><div class="mod-num"><small>Module</small><b>3</b></div><div class="mod-info"><h3>Classifying Public Debt</h3><p>The five ways public debt is classified, the difference between general government debt and public sector debt, and external versus domestic debt.</p><div class="mod-tags"><span>⏱️ ~30 minutes</span><span>🎯 4 objectives</span><span>🗂️ 5 slides</span></div></div><div class="mod-go"><span class="mod-status">Start →</span><span class="chev">›</span></div></div><div class="mod-bar" data-mid="m4" data-openmod="m4"><div class="mod-num"><small>Module</small><b>4</b></div><div class="mod-info"><h3>Gross vs Net Debt, Debt-to-GDP &amp; EAMU Convergence</h3><p>The headline debt numbers — gross versus net debt, the debt-to-GDP ratio, and the regional convergence ceiling.</p><div class="mod-tags"><span>⏱️ ~28 minutes</span><span>🎯 3 objectives</span><span>🗂️ 5 slides</span></div></div><div class="mod-go"><span class="mod-status">Start →</span><span class="chev">›</span></div></div><div class="mod-bar" data-mid="m5" data-openmod="m5"><div class="mod-num"><small>Module</small><b>5</b></div><div class="mod-info"><h3>Contingent Liabilities, Sustainability &amp; Restructuring</h3><p>Obligations that may arise, the indicators used to judge sustainability, and how rescheduling differs from restructuring.</p><div class="mod-tags"><span>⏱️ ~28 minutes</span><span>🎯 4 objectives</span><span>🗂️ 5 slides</span></div></div><div class="mod-go"><span class="mod-status">Start →</span><span class="chev">›</span></div></div><div class="assess-bar"><div class="ab-ic">🎓</div><div class="mod-info"class="course-inline-7"><h3>Final Assessment</h3><p>A shuffled set drawn from a large question bank — pass to earn your EAC certificate.</p></div><button class="btn btn-blue" data-screen="assessment">Start assessment →</button></div><div class="resources"><h3>📚 Other EAC statistics resources</h3><div class="res-links"><a class="res-link